{"path": "preprints/The-spherical-perceptron-with-bi-orthogonally-invariant-disorder-September-24-2026/build/paper.tex", "local": "frontier/sources/i14_spectral_width_novelty_r3/corpus/preprints/The-spherical-perceptron-with-bi-orthogonally-invariant-disorder-September-24-2026/build/paper.tex", "line": 1066, "text": "For $f\\in C_b(\\R)$ choose bounded Lipschitz approximants with a common bound and uniform convergence on compact intervals. Every angular configuration satisfies $M^{-1}\\sum_ry_r^2=\\sum_ja_j$. On a compact radius set, the fraction of entries outside $[-R,R]$ is uniformly $O(R^{-2})$. Thus compact approximation controls the normalized energy uniformly and transfers all angular conclusions. The same estimate applies to \\eqref{eq:softcoefficient} on a bounded operator-norm event, independently of $\\lambda,B,\\theta$, so its limiting formula has the same continuity. This completes the proof of Theorem~\\ref{thm:angular}."}
